nvidia-utils
# nvidia-open-dkms intentionally NOT here -- see commit message. DKMS builds
# its kernel module against whatever kernel is actually running, which on a
# live ISO can mean a build (or build attempt) happening at first boot on
# the target machine itself, not at ISO build time. On a VM with no real
# NVIDIA GPU for it to ever bind to, that's pure risk for zero benefit.
# nvidia-utils (userspace libs/EGL+Vulkan ICDs, no kernel module, no DKMS)
# stays -- it's inert without a matching kernel driver loaded.
